{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationConformance","type":"reference"},{"text":" runs the checks every vendor destination must pass, through a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ScriptedTransport","type":"reference"},{"text":" that keeps each request and answers from a script rather than the network:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"its requests match recorded fixtures byte for byte;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value is sent only after the adopter opts in, and only while the record reveals it;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"behind a tracker’s consent and ","type":"text"},{"code":"accepting(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", it sends exactly the records it is handed;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"a record over the vendor’s limit is left out and reported, and the rest of its batch is sent;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"no response, a 5xx, 408, 429 and each status of the encoder’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transientStatuses"},{"type":"text","text":" are retried,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and other failures are dropped and reported;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"a 2xx answer whose body the encoder can’t read, an empty one included, counts as delivered: sent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once, nothing reported;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"no request carries a trace context in its header fields, even while a tracer is active.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make it with the vendor’s limit and a closure that calls the vendor’s factory with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationSetup","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s plan, transport and backoff. Every check’s records are tracked at the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"setup’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp"},{"type":"text","text":"; a factory whose encoder leaves out records by their age takes it as the time"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it encodes at, so the checks pass whenever the test runs. Run each "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ConformanceCheck","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" as a test"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"case of its own:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import DestinationTesting","import Foundation","import HTTPDestinations","import PostHogEncoding","import Testing","","@Test(arguments: ConformanceCheck.allCases)","func postHogConformance(check: ConformanceCheck) async throws {","    let host = try #require(URL(string: \"https:\/\/posthog.example.com\"))","    let conformance = DestinationConformance(limit: PostHogBatchEncoder.batchLimit) { setup in","        try HTTPDestination.postHog(projectToken: \"phc_test\", host: host, plan: setup.plan, transport: setup.transport, backoff: setup.backoff)","    }","    try await conformance.expect(check)","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each check records a Swift Testing issue for every rule the destination breaks. A project’s own","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tests write their assertions out in full. This one is shared on purpose, as TrackingPlanTesting’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expectTrackingPlan(_:matches:sourceLocation:)"},{"text":" is, so every vendor module runs the same checks.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"It imports Swift Testing, so add it to test targets only. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"text":" leaves it out.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/writingavendordestination"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers the module these checks test.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"role":"collection","symbolKind":"module","externalID":"DestinationTesting","title":"DestinationTesting","roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"DestinationTesting"}]},"abstract":[{"text":"Check from Swift Testing that a vendor destination keeps the library’s rules and sends what its fixtures record.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationConformance","doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ConformanceCheck","doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationSetup"],"title":"Checking a destination","anchor":"Checking-a-destination"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ScriptedTransport"],"title":"Sending without a network","anchor":"Sending-without-a-network"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/destinationtesting"]}],"references":{"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting/DestinationSetup":{"type":"topic","title":"DestinationSetup","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DestinationSetup","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting\/destinationsetup","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DestinationSetup","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"What a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationConformance","isActive":true},{"text":" check hands the vendor’s factory: the plan of the events it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sends, the transport to send them through, a backoff short enough that a retry doesn’t hold the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"test up, and when its records were tracked.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationSetup"},"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting/ScriptedTransport":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScriptedTransport"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScriptedTransport"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ScriptedTransport","title":"ScriptedTransport","url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting\/scriptedtransport","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPTransport"},{"text":" that answers each request from a script and keeps every request it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sent: the seam a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationConformance","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" check sends through instead of the network.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting/DestinationConformance/expect(_:sourceLocation:)":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"expect","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"ConformanceCheck","preciseIdentifier":"s:18DestinationTesting16ConformanceCheckO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sourceLocation","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SourceLocation","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Testing14SourceLocationV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationConformance\/expect(_:sourceLocation:)","url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting\/destinationconformance\/expect(_:sourcelocation:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Records an issue for each way the destination breaks "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"check"},{"type":"text","text":"’s rule."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"expect(_:sourceLocation:)"},"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting":{"title":"DestinationTesting","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Check from Swift Testing that a vendor destination keeps the library’s rules and sends what its fixtures record."}],"url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting","role":"collection","kind":"symbol"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/writingavendordestination":{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/writingavendordestination","title":"Writing a Vendor Destination","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Writing a Vendor Destination","type":"text"}],"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent